README.md:46:# Run Maestro flows against your simulator
README.md:68:All UI automation runs through **GrantivaAgent** — a WebDriverAgent embedded in the CLI. No Accessibility permission needed, no Appium server, no Maestro install. Works headless on CI out of the box.
README.md:98:- **Concurrent runs** — Runs on different simulator UDIDs execute in parallel. Each simulator launches WebDriverAgent from its own runner home (`<runner home>/versions/<stamp>/devices/<udid>`, where the runner home is `GRANTIVA_RUNNER_HOME` or `~/.grantiva/runner` and `<stamp>` is the installed runner's stamp: the runner version plus the bundled Android driver tag, such as `1.1.28-grantiva.15+android-drivers-2`), which holds an APFS clone of the cached WDA build, so every run gets its own xctestrun, port, and DerivedData without rebuilding WDA. `simulator teardown` (with or without `--force`) and `simulator delete` remove the device's home under every installed `versions/<stamp>/`, and teardown exits non-zero naming any home it could not remove; homes of simulators that no longer exist are pruned on the next run. A second run targeting an already-owned simulator fails immediately with guidance to provision a unique simulator, protecting the active WDA session from cross-run teardown; when the owner is a `grantiva runner start` session the message says so and names `grantiva runner stop`. A run's lease file (`<runner home>/locks/<udid>.lock`) is removed when the run ends, and a deleted simulator's when it is deleted.
README.md:162:### Maestro Compatibility
README.md:164:Grantiva can read [Maestro](https://maestro.mobile.dev) flow files as a drop-in replacement. If you have existing Maestro flows, Grantiva will auto-detect and parse them — no rewrite needed.
README.md:168:Place your flows in a `.maestro/` directory, or write `grantiva.yml` in Maestro format:
README.md:182:Each `takeScreenshot` becomes a named screen capture point. Commands between screenshots become navigation steps. Supported Maestro commands: `tapOn`, `doubleTapOn`, `longPressOn`, `inputText`, `assertVisible`, `assertNotVisible`, `swipe` (`direction:`, optionally with `from:`, or `start:`/`end:` as `"x%, y%"`, plus `duration:`), `scroll`, `scrollUntilVisible` (kept as a scroll, with its `direction:` and `timeout:`), `runFlow` (a file, `{file: ...}`, or inline `{commands: [...]}`; a `takeScreenshot` inside a sub-flow is a screen like one in the parent), `extendedWaitUntil` (`visible:` or `notVisible:`, with its `timeout:` kept), `waitForAnimationToEnd`, `launchApp`, `stopApp`, `killApp`, and `takeScreenshot`. `grantiva-android.yml` may be written in the same Maestro format; its `appId:` is the application ID. Selectors accept a string or `{text: ...}` (matches text) or `{id: ...}` (matches the accessibility identifier). Any other command (`back`, scripting, permissions, etc.) is rejected before the run starts, with an error naming the file and line: `grantiva.yml:5: unsupported Maestro command 'back'`. Flows run with `grantiva run --flow` go to the runner as written and are not limited to this list.
README.md:340:grantiva run                Run Maestro flows against a simulator or emulator. No visual regression: reports step pass/fail and captures a screenshot on failure (see --keep-alive, --logs, --flow)
